{
  "abstract": "We give a conditional construction of rational Diophantine septuples from two anchors and an order-five compatibility cycle. The cycle supplies sixteen individual square roots. Imposing the classical regular-quintuple equation on its five tails recovers each of the five missing diagonal roots by an explicit polynomial identity. We describe a canonical genus-one source, its rational period-five map, and the precise squareclass matching needed to recover both anchor roots. The matching retains nontrivial source classes rather than requiring two factors to be squares separately. A rational sixteen-root example and a nondegenerate finite-field twenty-one-root example verify the constructions.\n\nWe then construct exact orbit and root-sign quotients. A further involution preserves every physical tail while exchanging the two correspondence parameters. At the inhabited anchor product $p=-4704/24025$, the resulting completion quotient is an irreducible curve of bidegree $(10,4)$. Exact discriminant and local Newton computations prove that its normalization has genus four and two rational points at infinity. The complete equation, construction algorithms and portable individual-root checks are supplied. Rational points on this quotient still require explicit source and anchor lifts. No rational point completing the construction has been found, and neither a rational septuple nor a rational-point classification is claimed.",
